  "name": "W2 · Upper gaps and benches (draft) – south-west pocket",
  "notes": "Job: the least-steep pockets and light gaps just below the lip (still about 24–28°, so bench each tree). Zone 3.\nAvocado just below the runoff basins (never in a wet hollow) – this is where the avocados from the SE goat trial go; white and black sapote; macadamia.\nKeep goats out of this pocket when the south-west goat zone starts (avocado is toxic to goats).\nMango only in the sunniest open gaps; bunya well away from paths and the house (falling cones).\nStart with a pioneer row of pigeon pea and cassava for shade, mulch and nitrogen.\nDragon fruit on posts in sunny gaps; pineapple as the low layer.\nPlant at the start of the wet; no irrigation planned.\nPlaced from the 2022 LiDAR (1 m): slope, flow lines and ground light.\nDraft from the 19–20 Oct western high edge plan – adjust on site.",
